Package: mfrmr
Type: Package
Title: Fast Estimation, Diagnostics, and Generalizability for
        Many-Facet Models
Version: 0.3.2
Date: 2026-11-26
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Ryuya", family = "Komuro", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "ryuya.komuro.c4@tohoku.ac.jp",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9205-0926"))
Description: Estimates many-facet ordered-response measurement models (Rating
    Scale, Partial Credit, and Generalized Many-Facet Rasch Models) including
    step constraints, declarative category support, explanatory facet
    covariates, and joint interactions via high-speed C++ Joint Maximum
    Likelihood, Jeffreys-penalized Joint Maximum Likelihood with Block-Schur
    standard errors, Gauss-Hermite and Laplace-adaptive Marginal Maximum
    Likelihood (with expected a posteriori scoring, Warm's weighted likelihood
    estimation, latent regression, and sandwich covariances), Conditional
    Maximum Likelihood, and Laplace empirical Bayes Markov rater drift models.
    Provides multi-threaded C++ batch estimation, connectivity audits prior to
    estimation, fit diagnostics, Fair(M), Real SE, 'RajuSA-Welch' pairwise bias
    and parallel split-element differential facet functioning,
    color-vision-safe 'ggplot2' graphics, and Generalizability (G-Study) and
    Decision (D-Study) planning including fast Henderson Method 1 ('urGENOVA')
    estimation. Connects calibration, diagnostics, visualizations, and
    Markdown, HTML, or Word report generation in one analysis workflow. See
    Andrich (1978) <doi:10.1007/BF02293814>, Masters (1982)
    <doi:10.1007/BF02296272>, Warm (1989) <doi:10.1007/BF02294627>, Raju
    (1990) <doi:10.1177/014662169001400208>, Uto and Ueno (2020)
    <doi:10.1007/s41237-020-00115-7>, and Brennan (2001, ISBN:9780387952826).
